      "source": "16 from the 'Part Number' column + 10 from 'Customer Part Number'; both ruled genuine affected-part columns in docs/pcn-corpus-validation-2026-09-21.md s1. The Customer column has 8 CELLS, two of which hold two part numbers each (comma+newline), so it contributes 10 PARTS. CORRECTED 2026-09-24 from count=24: the two composite cells were previously carried glued, which made this file assert that a two-part cell is one part. See _construction.",
      "manifest": "sustainment/inbound/generated/TYC-PCN-24-210412_pdf/manifest.json",
      "headers": {
        "_note": "HEADER ground truth, added 2026-09-30. Established from the page, not from a run: every value below is read off the source PDF's page 1, and the competing value each run produced is named so a future reader can tell a defect from a disagreement. TYC is the degraded-text-layer notice -- its layer drops the 'ti' ligature everywhere -- so for this notice the text layer is a KNOWN-DAMAGED source and may not settle a field by itself. Every field in this block is now established; there are no pending fields left here. (The `pending` status itself is NOT retired -- it is the mechanism that keeps an unestablished field out of both the pass and the fail column, and the next notice to get a headers block will need it.)",
        "mfr": {
          "value": "TE Connectivity",
          "source": "Page 1, centred heading directly under the TE logo: 'TE Connectivity'.",
          "accepted": {
            "_rule": "ACCEPTED-VERBATIM SET, ruled 2026-10-09. `value` above stays the CANONICAL form; every non-underscore key here is a verbatim-correct reading of THIS notice, and comparison is canonical-after-alias -- a written string is mapped to its canonical form FIRST, and only canonical forms are compared. A raw-string compare against `value` is the wrong comparator for a verbatim field, and it is what made the witness supplier score 0/3 with every answer correct: the witness read the logo, the text layer read its own damaged heading, and the comparator called two correct readings a disagreement. The set is CLOSED -- a spelling not listed here is not accounted for, which is what `wrong` reports. Keys here may not also appear in `not`; the scorer raises on an overlap rather than letting one block win.",
            "TE Connectivity": "The heading as the page prints it, and the canonical form.",
            "TE Connecvity": "The text layer's reading, with the 'ti' ligature dropped -- the same damage that classifies this notice as degraded. Under the mfr-verbatim rule this IS the string the source hands an extractor, so it is verbatim-correct and may not be scored as a miss. It is still not the canonical form and must never be written as one.",
            "TE": "The logo wordmark, which renders as 'TE' over 'connectivity'. This is what the vision witness reads off the page image, and it is a correct reading of what it was shown."
          },
          "not": {
            "_was": "'TE Connecvity' and 'TE' were carried HERE, as declared distractors, until 2026-10-09. That was wrong on its face for a verbatim field: each is a faithful reading of a real part of the page, so three fires picked three members of one accepted set and the gate called one of them a failure -- a verdict decided by which member came up, not by whether the extraction was right. Ruled: they are ALIASES, not distractors. This block is kept and left otherwise EMPTY rather than deleted, because an mfr distractor remains possible -- a manufacturer named nowhere on the page would be one -- and an empty block records that the question was asked."
          }
        },
        "pub_date": {
          "value": "2024-06-07",
          "source": "Page 1, right-hand field: 'PCN Date: 07-JUN-24'.",
          "not": {
            "2024-06-10": "The portal's print stamp -- 'Current Date: 10-Jun-2024' in the top-right rule, and '6/10/24, 11:28 AM' in the browser print header. It is the date the PDF was rendered, NOT the date the notice was published. Unpinned fires flipped between the two, which is what this entry exists to adjudicate."
          }
        },
        "doc_level_ltb_date": {
          "value": "2024-06-06",
          "source": "Page 1, 'Estimated Dates' table, row 'Last Order Date (Obsolete Parts Only):' -> '06-JUN-2024'. ESTABLISHED 2026-09-30 by rendering page 1 of the source PDF at 500 DPI (pypdfium2) and reading the table region directly -- not from a run, and not from the text layer, which for this notice is a known-damaged source. The whole date surface of that table was read at the same time, so the 'not' block below is CLOSED rather than a sample: 'Last Ship Date of Changed Items (Obsolete Parts Only): 07-JUN-2024'; 'First Ship Date of Changed Items' blank; 'Last Date for Mixed Shipments: No Mixed Shipments'; 'Effectivity Date' and 'Date of First Samples' both blank. The only other dates anywhere on the page are 'PCN Date: 07-JUN-24' and the portal print stamp, both already adjudicated under pub_date.",
          "not": {
            "2024-06-07": "The ADJACENT ROW -- 'Last Ship Date of Changed Items (Obsolete Parts Only)'. A real date on the real page, one row below the right one, and it is also the correct pub_date, so a run returning it has either taken the wrong row of this table or copied the PCN date. The row label is what distinguishes them; the value cannot.",
            "2024-06-08": "The second witness's reading of the page image. This date appears NOWHERE on the page -- not in this table, not in any other field. It is a digit substitution by the vision model, the standing failure mode for that witness, so agreeing with it would be agreeing with a fabrication. Recorded here because it was carried as a live candidate until the page was read."
          }
        }
      }
    },
